    pr_ref:  # ed22
    description: "Discovered 2026-04-19 during WI-noraf investigation: websocket_handler is mapped to WEBSOCKET_HANDLER at entrypoints.py:425-439 (since ADR-0003 v0.9.x) but shows inert in docs/CONCEPTS.md. Root cause is regex coverage, not missing code.\n\n**Known false-inert concepts** from packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/entrypoints.py grep:\nerror_handler, websocket_handler, websocket_gateway, event_handler, middleware, command, liveview, graphql_resolver, graphql_schema, lifecycle_hook, main_function, main_guard, library_export, serialization_callback, controller_by_name, handler_by_name, broker_lifecycle_by_name, service_by_name, command_by_name, entrypoint, app_bootstrap, ipc_handler, application, npm_bin, cargo_binary, pyproject_script.\n\n**Proposed fix:**\n1. Broaden == regex to match any identifier containing 'concept': \\\\b\\\\w*concept\\\\w*\\\\s*==\\\\s*[\"'](\\\\w+)[\"']\n2. Add regex for tuple-membership: concept-var in (...) then scan tuple body for quoted identifiers.\n3. Mirror for != (exclusion patterns).\n4. Regenerate docs/CONCEPTS.md — expect a large inert→live flip.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- error_handler, websocket_handler, controller, middleware, event_handler all show 'live' after regeneration.\n- No false ghost classifications introduced.\n- Unit tests added for the regex additions (script has none today)."  # ed22
    fields:  # ed22
      statement: "docs/CONCEPTS.md status column (live/inert/ghost) must accurately reflect whether a concept has at least one code consumer; every concept_type == \"X\" or concept_type in (\"X\", \"Y\") pattern in hypergumbo-core source must count as a consumer."  # ed22
      root_cause: "scripts/generate-concepts consumer-detection regex only matches bare-name concept == \"X\", not variable-name patterns like concept_type == \"X\", and never matches tuple-membership tests like concept_type in (\"X\", \"Y\"). The ~30 concepts consumed in entrypoints._detect_from_concepts via concept_type variable are all false-inert in docs/CONCEPTS.md."  # ed22
